Automating Build and Test with Jenkins
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Install and configure Jenkins on a Linux machine
Create and configure Jenkins pipelines using a Jenkinsfile
Define build, test, and packaging stages in a Jenkins pipeline
Automate the build process for a Java application using Maven
Implement automated testing and code coverage reporting after the build stage
Configure real, working build notifications using logging and email
Monitor, troubleshoot, and analyze Jenkins pipeline executions
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with the Git version control system
Basic knowledge of Java programming and the Maven build tool
Understanding of software development lifecycle concepts
Experience with text editors such as nano or vim
