Subtask 5.3: Monitor Build Trends
From the jenkins-demo-pipeline job page, click Build History in the left sidebar
Observe the sequence of build results (blue/green for success, red for failure) across your last several builds, corresponding to the passing build, the deliberate failure, and the recovery build
Click on any individual build number to open its Console Output and compare execution times reported at the bottom of the log (Finished: SUCCESS line includes elapsed time)
Open Test Result Trend (visible on the job's main page once at least two builds have run) to view a graph of passed versus failed tests across builds
Note which build number introduced the failure and which build number restored a passing state â this history is the basis for diagnosing regressions in a real CI/CD workflow
Deliverable: A jenkins-demo-pipeline build history containing at least three builds: one passing, one failing (red, stopped at Unit Tests), and one passing again, with the Test Result Trend graph visibly showing the dip and recovery in passed test count.

